  <h2>Where AI actually helps in civil engineering</h2>
  <p>Most of the time savings from AI on a civil project come from <strong>document drafting</strong>, <strong>code lookup</strong>, and <strong>multi-option exploration</strong> — not from the engineer's core calculations. A licensed PE still has to stamp the hydrology, the grading, and the SWPPP. What AI does well is take a rough scope, your firm's standards, and a code reference and turn them into a first draft you can react to. That's where this guide starts.</p>

  <p><em>Official references:</em> <a href="https://www.epa.gov/npdes/stormwater-discharges-construction-activities" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">EPA NPDES Construction Stormwater</a> · <a href="https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/engineering/hydraulics/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">FHWA Hydraulic Engineering</a> · <a href="https://ascelibrary.org/journal/jhyeff" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ASCE Journal of Hydraulic Engineering</a></p>

